Title: Keep self-registering objects (formats, extensions) when linking on AROS
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: File formats, script extensions and other parts register themselves through static objects in app-lib and delta. Those archive members are only linked with --whole-archive, which src/CMakeLists.txt enables for UNIX, MinGW, Apple and MSVC; CMake does not set UNIX for AROS, so they were dropped and saving reported 'LibreSprite can''t save "png" files'.
Change: Use --whole-archive on AROS too.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: candidate
Verification: mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16 (see the patch series record)
Removal: when upstream treats AROS like other GNU-ld systems.
---
diff --git a/src/CMakeLists.txt b/src/CMakeLists.txt
index 86e8aa8cf33af28c149159a12563f950b40c6ed7..7448f653e790c3a0793c38ab9a844b2c0f0c31b8 100644
--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ endif(MSVC)
 # Directories where .h files can be found
 include_directories(. .. ../third_party ../third_party/observable)
 
-if((UNIX AND NOT APPLE) OR (WIN32 AND NOT MSVC))
+if((UNIX AND NOT APPLE) OR (WIN32 AND NOT MSVC) OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "AROS")
   set(KEEP_INJECTIONS_BEGIN "-Wl,--whole-archive")
   set(KEEP_INJECTIONS_END "-Wl,--no-whole-archive")
 endif()
